        <!-- Section: Which Date Should You Count Down To in a Multi-Day Wedding? -->
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#B76E79] uppercase tracking-wider">Multi-Day Planning</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#1A1A1A]" style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;">
              Which Date Should You Count Down To in a Multi-Day Wedding?
            </h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
            Count down to the first day that needs full planning, usually the first big function, and treat the main ceremony as a milestone.
          </p>
          <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
            Many Pakistani, Indian and wider South Asian weddings run across several days, with functions such as a mehndi, sangeet, baraat, nikah and walima. A countdown points at one date, so there's no perfect pick. Choosing the first function means venues, decor and travel all get planned against the earliest deadline. Choosing the main ceremony feels more natural but can leave the early events short of time.
          </p>

          <div class="my-6">
            <img
              src="/Multi-Day South Asian Wedding.webp"
              alt="Multi-day South Asian wedding celebration timeline and bridal planning"
              class="w-full rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-[#F3E8EA] object-cover"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
            <p class="text-center text-xs text-slate-500 mt-2 italic">
              Multi-day celebrations require anchoring your countdown to the earliest function on your calendar.
            </p>
          </div>

          <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
            Our <a href="/checklists/pakistani-wedding-checklist" class="text-[#B76E79] font-bold underline hover:text-[#a25d66]">Pakistani & Muslim Multi-Day Checklist</a> and <a href="/checklists/indian-wedding-checklist" class="text-[#B76E79] font-bold underline hover:text-[#a25d66]">Indian Wedding Master Checklist</a> break the days into functions, so you can plan each one on its own.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Section: How Can You Share Your Countdown With Family and Friends? -->
        <div class="space-y-4">
