            <div class="p-4 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm">
              <strong class="text-[#1A1A1A] block mb-1">Watching instead of doing.</strong>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">A ticking clock doesn't book a caterer. Attach one action to every check.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm">
              <strong class="text-[#1A1A1A] block mb-1">Counting to the wrong date.</strong>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">For multi-day weddings, decide on the anchor date early, as covered above.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm">
              <strong class="text-[#1A1A1A] block mb-1">Skipping buffers.</strong>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Set your own deadlines two to three weeks ahead of vendor cutoffs.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm">
              <strong class="text-[#1A1A1A] block mb-1">Treating a short countdown as failure.</strong>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Fewer days means fewer, faster decisions. It doesn't mean a worse wedding.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-[#F3E8EA] shadow-sm">
              <strong class="text-[#1A1A1A] block mb-1">Forgetting to update.</strong>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">If the date moves, change the countdown the same day and re-share the card, so nobody keeps working from the old number.</p>
            </div>
